{
  "challenges": [
    {
      "publicId": "chal_coding_pdp_152",
      "name": "restaurant-commission-history",
      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Keep the history of restaurant commissions",
      "description": "Finance recomputed September's commission with October's rates because `dim_restaurant` was overwritten every night. The editor holds `pipelines/dim_restaurant_scd2.py` with its key blocks missing, each marked by a `# [ ]` line; some pieces are wrong on purpose. Fill every line so that a change of `district` or `commission_pct` closes the current version on the snapshot's date and opens a new one, a new `name` corrects every version without creating one, a new restaurant gets its first version, applying the same snapshot twice changes nothing, and `restaurant_sk_at` returns the version valid on a given day (`valid_from <= day < valid_to`). Run applies a series of snapshots on SQLite, then prices orders with the version valid on their day.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "outcomes": [
        "modeling"
      ],
      "points": 40,
      "hints": [
        "Draw one restaurant's timeline: two versions with `valid_from` and `valid_to`, and an order on 30 September and one on 1 October. Which version must each order find, and which date ends the first version?",
        "Look at the current row (`is_current = 1`), a tuple comparison of only the tracked attributes, an `UPDATE` that ends a version on the snapshot's date, and a lookup with `valid_from <= ? AND ? < valid_to`.",
        "A product dimension that tracks `category` but not `description` would do: `if new.description != cur.description: UPDATE ... SET description = ? WHERE product_id = ?`, then `if (new.category,) != (cur.category,): UPDATE ... SET valid_to = :day, is_current = 0 WHERE product_sk = :sk` followed by an INSERT with `valid_from = :day`."
      ],
      "coding": {
        "language": "python",
        "filePath": "pipelines/dim_restaurant_scd2.py",
        "executionMode": "stdio",
        "timeLimitMs": 3000,
        "memoryLimitMb": 128,
        "scoringMode": "all_or_nothing",
        "maxAttempts": null
      },
